From: lutvzn <106083845+lutvzn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:30:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] qualcommax: ipq50xx: redmi-ax3000: enable the temperature
 sensor

TSENS was disabled because the boot firmware does not turn it on and
some zones were said to report bogus critical temperatures. The upstream
driver enables the block itself on the IPQ5018 (init_tsens_v1_no_rpm),
and this IPQ5000 has a two-point calibration fused (mode 3). Read on the
board with the same enable sequence: s1-s4 (ubi32, cpu, top-glue, gephy)
at 62-63 C idle, 68 C after 4 minutes of both cores at 100 %, back to
64 C two minutes later; the zones agree within 1 C.

This gives the cpu-thermal passive trip (100 C, cpufreq cooling) and the
120 C critical trips from ipq5018.dtsi, and temperatures in
/sys/class/thermal and hwmon.
---
 .../qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts   | 25 +++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts b/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts
index 5fdcde3792..9f3ff0a452 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts
@@ -112,12 +112,12 @@
 
 /*
  * Keep the CPU at the rated 1008 MHz, the highest operating point of the
- * vendor firmware (800 and 1008 MHz at 1.1 V). There is no CPU regulator,
- * and with TSENS off (below) no thermal throttling either. Boosting to
- * 1296 MHz at the same 1.1 V corrupted memory on this IPQ5000 under
- * network load: single bits cleared (mostly bit 42 of a 64-bit word),
- * kernel oopses on pointers and silent resets every few minutes, none
- * at 1008 MHz.
+ * vendor firmware (800 and 1008 MHz at 1.1 V). There is no CPU regulator.
+ * Boosting to 1296 MHz at the same 1.1 V corrupted memory on this IPQ5000
+ * under network load: single bits cleared (mostly bit 42 of a 64-bit
+ * word), kernel oopses on pointers and silent resets every few minutes,
+ * none at 1008 MHz. It is not thermal: with the CPU pinned at 1296 MHz
+ * the board reset 1.5 s into the load, and it idles at about 63 C.
  */
 &cpu_opp_table {
 	/delete-node/ opp-1296000000;
@@ -156,13 +156,16 @@
 };
 
 /*
- * TSENS is not enabled by the boot firmware on this IPQ5000 ("tsens
- * device is not enabled" with the vendor kernel) and some of its zones
- * report bogus critical temperatures, which shuts the board down early
- * in boot. Keep it off.
+ * The boot firmware leaves TSENS off ("tsens device is not enabled" with
+ * the vendor kernel), but the upstream driver turns it on itself on the
+ * IPQ5018 (no RPM). The IPQ5000 fuses hold a two-point calibration, and
+ * the zones read 62-63 C idle in the closed case and 68 C after 4 min
+ * of both cores at 100 %, all within 1 C of each other. This brings the
+ * cpu-thermal throttling (100 C) and critical shutdown (120 C) trips of
+ * ipq5018.dtsi.
  */
 &tsens {
-	status = "disabled";
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &qpic_bam {
